      "content": "It is crucial to recognize that melanoma can present differently across various skin tones, making standard visual cues less reliable for all patients. In individuals with darker skin, melanoma may appear as a darker brown or black lesion instead of the typical red or brown spots seen in lighter skin. Furthermore, progression can sometimes be subtle, so clinicians must be highly vigilant for any new or changing pigment irregularities in all racial groups. Always remember that the ABCDEs framework should be applied with awareness of skin pigmentation differences.",
